@title Month-end close runbook
@subtitle Finance operations, Tallow & Brook Distribution
@author Controller
@date 2026-10-01

kpi Target | 5 working days | to close the books | good
kpi Books lock | day 5, 12:00 | Controller signs off | bad
kpi Controller | Marcus Eldridge | owner of this runbook

!!! The books lock at 12:00 on day 5. Nothing is posted after that without an approved reopen request.

## Calendar

data close = task,start,end; Day 1 cut-off and bank reconciliations,1,2; Day 2 accruals and inventory,2,3; Day 3 intercompany and payroll,3,4; Day 4 variance review,4,5; Day 5 sign-off and lock,5,6
chart range close from=start to=end title="Close calendar by working day"

step Cut off sales and purchasing at 17:00; finish bank reconciliations | Day 1
step Post accruals and depreciation; reconcile inventory to the warehouse count | Day 2
step Eliminate intercompany balances between the three legal entities; reconcile payroll | Day 3
step Review variances | Day 4
step Controller signs off; books lock at 12:00 | Day 5

## Before sign-off

kpi Checks to pass | 5 | before sign-off

- [ ] Every balance sheet account is reconciled.
- [ ] Any reconciling difference is under $50 or explained.
- [ ] Variances over 5% and over $10,000 each have a written explanation.
- [ ] Intercompany balances net to zero.
- [ ] The trial balance debits equal credits.

## If a deadline slips

!! If day 5 will be missed by more than 1 working day, notify the CFO, Valentina Sokolov.

1. Tell the Controller the same day.
2. Decide whether the slip delays sign-off. If day 5 will be missed by more than 1 working day, notify the CFO, Valentina Sokolov.
3. Do not post late entries after the lock without a reopen request signed by the Controller.
4. Record the cause in the close log.

